826b3c0b6c6f35f589d1afa29d3242b77e2d2de8e4a7dea759ef7a436dc4989&node=scalar.separate_classical_algorithm&relation=direct","prerequisite_uses":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=d826b3c0b6c6f35f589d1afa29d3242b77e2d2de8e4a7dea759ef7a436dc4989&node=scalar.separate_classical_algorithm&relation=prerequisites","prerequisites":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=d826b3c0b6c6f35f589d1afa29d3242b77e2d2de8e4a7dea759ef7a436dc4989&view=arguments&node=scalar.separate_classical_algorithm&assumptions=true"},"neighborhood_href":"/api/v1/neighborhood?manifest=d826b3c0b6c6f35f589d1afa29d3242b77e2d2de8e4a7dea759ef7a436dc4989&ref=sha256%3A05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0%2Fnodes%2Fscalar.separate_classical_algorithm","record":{"assumption_ids":[],"boundary":"A distinct consequence using the external algorithm theorem and attained minimizer. It is not the source of the QAOA rooted Gaussian energy identity and does not imply efficient angle selection or finite-precision/preprocessing complexity.","citation_ids":["scalar-r2-26-cite-separate-classical-algorithm","scalar-r2-26-cite-eams-algorithm"],"evidence_ids":[],"id":"scalar.separate_classical_algorithm","kind":"claim","label":"Separate finite-disorder optimization consequence","locator":"algorithm-application.tex:1–59; cor:algorithm","source_id":"scalar-r2-26-source-algorithm-application","statement":"For every fixed epsilon>0, choose an attained minimizer gamma₀ using Auffinger–Chen. Apply the conditional full-support theorem to this witness to obtain strict increase, and then EAMS arXiv:2001.00904v1 Assumption 2, Theorem 3 and Corollary 2.2. This gives a randomized finite-spin output within epsilon n of max H_n with probability tending to one over both Gaussian disorder and algorithmic randomness and at most C(epsilon)n² real-arithmetic operations in the stated oracle/preprocessing model. The chosen minimizer is locally bound in this application, not a caller-supplied premise.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/nodes/scalar.separate_classical_algorithm","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/nodes/scalar.separate_classical_algorithm","id":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/edges/%5B%22scalar.separate_classical_algorithm%22%2C%22scalar.minimizer_attainment%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/edges/%5B%22scalar.separate_classical_algorithm%22%2C%22scalar.minimizer_attainment%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","semantic_class":"curated_argument_support","to":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/nodes/scalar.minimizer_attainment"},{"application":{"premise_bindings":[{"assumption_id":"scalar.paper_minimizer","binding_names":["gamma"],"rationale":"Attainment supplies this same gamma_0 in the manuscript class U, with its admissibility and minimality, before applying the conditional full-support theorem.","supplier_id":"scalar.minimizer_attainment"},{"assumption_id":"scalar.paper_admissible","binding_names":["gamma"],"rationale":"Attainment supplies this same gamma_0 in the manuscript class U, with its admissibility and minimality, before applying the conditional full-support theorem.","supplier_id":"scalar.minimizer_attainment"}],"rationale":"The algorithm proof applies thm:full-support to a minimizer to obtain the EAMS no-overlap-gap input. Attainment is supplied separately by the manuscript main.tex:94–107 and the existing scalar.minimizer_attainment support. The same attained gamma_0 is used for full support and strict increase. This authored application records the full-support input only, not a proof or formalization of the external algorithm theorem.","remaining_assumption_ids":[],"shared_bindings":{"gamma":"one attained manuscript minimizer gamma_0 in U, kept fixed for full support and the external EAMS theorem"},"source_span":{"end_line":34,"source_id":"scalar-r2-26-source-algorithm-application","start_line":29},"status":"authored"},"application_metadata_scope":"remaining_assumption_ids is authored historical metadata, not an effective obligation audit; path-local suppression may be lifted for retained formal dependencies.","derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/nodes/scalar.separate_classical_algorithm","id":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/edges/%5B%22scalar.separate_classical_algorithm%22%2C%22support.full_relative_support%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/edges/%5B%22scalar.separate_classical_algorithm%22%2C%22support.full_relative_support%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","semantic_class":"curated_argument_support","to":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/nodes/support.full_relative_support"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/evidence/R2-26-SR-044","id":"field:29b2481604167871c48dec6c47514489d0440e76d8cd2bc1f7d068457e080512","kind":"subject_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/evidence/R2-26-SR-044","semantic_class":"provenance_field_reference","source_field":"subject_ids","to":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/nodes/scalar.separate_classical_algorithm"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/edges/%5B%22scalar.separate_classical_algorithm%22%2C%22support.full_relative_support%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","id":"field:5cbc3c78939aa952a9b8eaf8ab0f1efb2593b84a98b48c0028465b38038c8bc7","kind":"from","owner_ref":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6d